{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2999","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2999","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2999\",\"parent_revision\":\"83e144977889412430ac1998b0ad2f02beb3e2a272c133b2c5ad164e4c6d1833\",\"root_revision\":\"83e144977889412430ac1998b0ad2f02beb3e2a272c133b2c5ad164e4c6d1833\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_add`/`operations.py`'s `add_item()` (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py`, function ending ~line 1434) builds its response dict unconditionally, but only adds the `item_ref` key inside `if issue_ref:` (lines 1432-1433: `if issue_ref: result[\\\"item_ref\\\"] = issue_ref`) \u2014 then returns `{**result, **out.to_dict()}` regardless of whether `issue_ref` was ever set. So when GitHub issue creation fails or is skipped inside this function (the exact failure mode observed in the `test-e2e` CI job \u2014 see run `32122651665`, error: `AssertionError: Expected item_ref in result, got: ['title','priority','reference','file_path','messages','warnings','errors']`), `add_item()` returns a response with no `error` key, no exception raised, and a shape indistinguishable from a fully successful call except for the absence of one optional key. Any caller (agent or human) that doesn't specifically check for `item_ref`'s presence will treat this as a successful create and move on \u2014 a direct violation of this repo's own `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` (\\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" / \\\"Functions that perform side effects must return a value indicating what changed\\\").\\n\\nThis is not hypothetical: it is the live, current root cause of `test-e2e` failing on 100% of sampled recent pushes to `main` (`gh run list --workflow code-quality.yml --event push --limit 15` on 2026-08-18 showed 15/15 failures) \u2014 meaning the primary local-only-create path (no GitHub issue actually created) is being exercised in CI and its result is being asserted against, but the underlying contract (does `item_ref` always appear, or is its absence itself the signal of a degraded/local-only create) has never been made explicit or enforced.\\n\\nSeparately, the same `test-e2e` job's cleanup script also fails: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'httpx'` \u2014 meaning any GitHub-backed test issues created during a failed or interrupted e2e run are never cleaned up, leaking sandbox issues over time.\\n\\n**Root cause to fix:** decide and enforce an explicit contract for `add_item()`'s return shape \u2014 either `item_ref` is always present (using a well-defined sentinel/None for the local-only-create case) with an explicit field distinguishing \\\"created a GitHub issue\\\" from \\\"created a local-only item,\\\" or the function raises/returns an explicit error field when GitHub-backed creation was requested but did not succeed, per this repo's `silent-failure-prevention.md`. Also fix the cleanup script's missing `httpx` dependency (likely a PEP 723 inline-metadata gap \u2014 check the script's dependency block per this repo's Python conventions).\\n\\nThis is a P0, not a P1 or P2: it is a live, currently-reproducing silent-failure bug in the primary backlog-item write path (`backlog_add`), the single most-used entry point in the entire harness, and it is the root cause underlying issue #2991 (the `test-e2e` CI signal-integrity bug) \u2014 reference #2991 as related/blocking context here, but this item is scoped specifically to the `operations.py` contract bug and the cleanup script's missing dependency, not to the CI-wiring question #2991 already covers.\\n\\nRelated: #2991 (test-e2e job lacks continue-on-error, making this silent-failure bug's noisy but non-blocking manifestation turn every main CI run red).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `add_item()` return contract made explicit: `item_ref` always present (sentinel/None for local-only) with a field distinguishing GitHub-backed vs local-only create, OR an explicit `error` field is returned/raised when GitHub-backed creation was requested but did not succeed\\n- [ ] `test-e2e`'s cleanup script's missing `httpx` dependency fixed (PEP 723 metadata gap)\\n- [ ] A test specifically demonstrates the new/fixed behavior (per this repo's \\\"Close criteria\\\" convention \u2014 passing pre-existing tests is not sufficient)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **backlog_add's operations.py contract to make item_ref presence/absence an explicit, enforced signal** so that **a failed or local-only GitHub issue create is never indistinguishable from a fully successful one**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: CI investigation of test-e2e failures on main (2026-08-18/19), companion item referenced by issue #2991\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Process note**: automated grooming via `/dh:work-backlog-item create` could not run \u2014 that skill's `<gate_token>` bang-exec (`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"`) failed reproducibly in this session (`Shell command failed for pattern \\\"!`...`\\\": [stderr] (eval):1: permission denied: ../..`, reproduced 3x including on a bare `--help`, and on the redirect-alternate `/dh:create-backlog-item`). A manually-generated gate token (running the identical script directly, which succeeds standalone) was correctly rejected by `backlog_add`'s server-side gate check, confirming the gate validates more than token-file presence \u2014 no further bypass was attempted. This item was filed via `gh issue create` directly as the legitimate fallback. See the companion item filed alongside this one, documenting the skill breakage itself.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"74760886c41312bc5345a3c19b52d524f8275aad47dc1cc906731cda338a7b97\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIROQ\"}"}